{#
/**
 * @file
 * Person node template — `front` view mode ONLY.
 *
 * Renders the homepage About section. The person node is pulled in as the
 * homepage's mainEntity: page.schema_main_entity → entity_reference_entity_view
 * formatter in the `front` view mode (see core.entity_view_display.node.page
 * .default), which fires this node--person--front suggestion. The page template
 * prints it via {{ content.schema_main_entity|field_value }} (the field wrapper
 * + "Main Entity" label are stripped there).
 *
 * ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
 * ║ PURE MARKUP. label/title/skills are built upstream in the preprocess hook ║
 * ║   includes/node.theme → surface_preprocess_node__person__front()          ║
 * ║ into the `about` variable. body is the one value resolved Twig-side (the  ║
 * ║ documented |field_value|render pattern strips the field wrapper).         ║
 * ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
 *
 * Why label/title come from the hook (not this template):
 *   `node` here is the PERSON, which holds the bio (body) + skills
 *   (schema_knows_about). The About eyebrow + heading live on the PAGE
 *   (field_about_label / field_about_title) — a person can't see page context,
 *   so the hook reads them off the routed page node. See the hook for detail.
 *
 * @see surface_preprocess_node__person__front()
 * @see @components/about/about.twig  (slots: label, title, skills[], body)
 */
#}
{% include '@components/about/about.twig' with {
  'label':  about.label,
  'title':  about.title,
  'skills': about.skills,
  'body':   content.body|field_value,
} only %}
